  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "The secondhand dry bulk market is fiercely tight. Panamax rates have been consistently \nimproving, and Chinese appetite for overage tonnage is driving prices. The Chinese buyers are willing \nto pay up and seem to be setting new benchmarks week on week.  \n \nIt is important to note that asset prices for 15-year-old Japanese tonnage are even more inflated, which \nis pulling up the values of older ships - In the Eco segment the market has become extremely firm, \nhence smaller players are reluctant to invest in younger/significantly more expensive bulkers despite \nthe need to increase capacity for Far Eastern trades. \n \nThis week, we recorded a total of 12 transactions, comprising 1 Capesize, 1 post-panamax, 1 \nKamsarmax, 1 Panamax, 2 Supramax, and 6 Handysize bulk carriers. For a detailed review and \nadditional information regarding these transactions, kindly refer to our \"representative sales\" section.",
    "demolition": "The Subcontinent markets remain same as last week with minimal activity. For an \noverview of demolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
